// "Amass [subtype] N" [CR#701.47a] — the canonical *composite* keyword action:
// it names no new engine primitive, it DECOMPOSES into ones the grammar already
// carries. Verbatim ([CR#701.47a]): "If you don't control an Army creature,
// create a 0/0 black [subtype] Army creature token. Choose an Army creature you
// control. Put N +1/+1 counters on that creature. If it isn't a [subtype], it
// becomes a [subtype] in addition to its other types."
//
// The four sentences map one-for-one onto core:
//   1. `If(Not(Exists(Army creature you control)), Create(... token ...))` — the
//      guard token, a 0/0 black creature whose subtypes are the amassed
//      `${0}` (forwarded whole as the declared subtype's expansion) PLUS
//      `Army`.
//   2. `With(ChooseOne(Army creature you control), …)` — bind the chosen Army as
//      `That` for the two clauses that follow. A `With` one-binder
//      (`ChooseOne`) binds its pick as `Reference::That`, never `It` (the
//      engine sets only `anaphora.that` for a `With`; `It` is the ITERATION
//      anaphor of a divide/`Each`, a different slot, and would fizzle unbound
//      here). The chosen "Army creature" spells `That(Creature)`. (After step 1
//      the token, if made, is itself an Army creature you control, so the
//      choice is always satisfiable.)
//   3. `PutCounters(That, P1P1Counter, ${1})` — the growth.
//   4. `If(Not(Matches(That, ${0})), Continuously(Modify(That, add ${0}), EndOfGame))`
//      — "becomes a [subtype] in addition": a one-shot-created continuous effect
//      with no stated duration ([CR#611.2a]) that adds the subtype, guarded so a
//      creature that is already that subtype is untouched.
//
// `${0}` is the amassed subtype (a declared `Subtype`, e.g. `Zombie`), which
// macro-expands to the full declared def — a `Subtype` struct in the token
// type-line, a bare-name `SubtypeRef` in the `Matches` filter and the layer-4
// `Subtypes(Add(...))`. An undeclared name has no subtype macro and fails to
// parse (validation for free). `${1}` is N (a `Count`). An `OneShotEffect`-kind
// macro, so `Amass(Zombie, 1)` stands as the effect body of any shell — an ETB
// trigger, an activated ability, or a spell.
(
    name: "Amass",
    template: "amass ${0} ${1}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Subtype, Count],
    body: Sequentially([
        If(
            condition: Not(Exists(And([
                Type(Creature),
                Subtype(Army),
                ControlledBy(Ref(You)),
            ]))),
            then: Create(1, Token(
                color_indicator: [Black],
                types: [Creature],
                subtypes: [
                    Param(0),
                    Army,
                ],
                power: 0,
                toughness: 0,
            )),
        ),
        With(
            binder: ChooseOne(filter: And([
                Type(Creature),
                Subtype(Army),
                ControlledBy(Ref(You)),
            ])),
            body: Sequentially([
                PutCounters(That(Creature), P1P1Counter, Param(1)),
                If(
                    condition: Not(Matches(That(Creature), Subtype(Param(0)))),
                    then: Continuously(
                        effect: Modify(That(Creature), Subtypes(Add(Param(0)))),
                        duration: EndOfGame,
                    ),
                ),
            ]),
        ),
    ]),
)
